    "updated_at": "2025-03-08T19:08:07Z",
    "body": "Different Dom(e|i)nic here, but I'm curious about the \"browser support\". You marked all browsers as supportive in https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/1807, and I can't really imagine a browser being supportive of that overall effort but objecting on this PR's supplementary bit. I guess my general question is: are all browsers supportive of what exists in https://privacycg.github.io/storage-access/ (https://privacycg.github.io/storage-access/#ua-state specifically)?\r\n\r\nSecond, should we expect another PR similar to this one to upstream the same bit for [\"source snapshot params\"](https://privacycg.github.io/storage-access/#source-snapshot-params-has-storage-access)? What are the plans for that?\r\n\r\n> This patch adds the bit, which remains false, and does nothing.\r\n\r\nThis is true from the perspective of the universe of WHATWG standards. But it'd be good to clarify in the commit message/OP that the purpose of this PR is to expose something that _will be_ [manipulated and set to true](https://privacycg.github.io/storage-access/#ref-for-environment-has-storage-access%E2%91%A1) from _other specifications_, and just needs to appear here so that Fetch can reference it directly.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
