    "updated_at": "2025-05-19T13:42:21Z",
    "body": "To be concrete about why I'm scared we might get stuck halfway:\r\n\r\n- This PR could land quickly\r\n- https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/1807 has a lot of review still happening, and says it depends on not just this PR, but 3 HTML PRs\r\n- One of the other HTML PRs is https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8036, which seems like it will need a good amount more work and doesn't have a clear owner at this point. Edit: this is now https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11133.\r\n- The other HTML PR is https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10991 which has a \"thing we identified that's worth looking into\" which I'm unsure how hard it will be to resolve.\r\n\r\nAgain, I'm happy to delegate this, but I just want to voice this concern.\r\n\r\nThe alternative model would be having synchronized PRs ready across HTML, Fetch, and Storage Access API, all landable within the same day, with the Storage Access API PRs being removal PRs that remove anything that's now redundant with HTML + Fetch.",
